# Korean presets: Hangul in Paperlogy, numerals and Latin in Inter. Inter
# leads the explicit family list and Paperlogy follows for per-glyph
# fallback (see base.mplstyle for why font.family must be explicit, not the
# generic `sans-serif`). Paperlogy led until #821, but its digits are
# fixed-width (0.667 em) and unkerned, so "−15" read "−1 5"; Inter's
# stems match Paperlogy's at the presets' weights (200, 400, 500, 700).
# Mathtext draws the text around "$…$" in the first family only, and Inter
# has no Hangul: dm.simple_layout gives such a text Paperlogy first
# (font/mathface.py). font.sans-serif is held IDENTICAL to font.family:
# bundled families only, no machine-dependent OS fonts.
font.family: Inter, Paperlogy, Noto Sans CJK KR, Pretendard, Noto Sans Math, Noto Sans Symbols, Noto Sans Symbols 2, sans-serif
font.sans-serif: Inter, Paperlogy, Noto Sans CJK KR, Pretendard, Noto Sans Math, Noto Sans Symbols, Noto Sans Symbols 2, sans-serif
